      <aadc:feature_type_name>Landing</aadc:feature_type_name>
      <aadc:narrative>The old airstrip on blue ice above Mawson.</aadc:narrative>
      <aadc:named_for>1979 place name minutes show "The name 'Gwamm' is made up of the initials of the wives and sweethearts of the officers and airmen of the 1958 RAAF Antarctic Flight. * The name was considered inappropriate because of its obscure and private origin. It was felt that the ice runway needs a name." The name wasn't approved.&#13;
&#13;
1994 place name minutes show "There is a need for a name for the old airstrip on blue ice above Mawson.&#13;
It was named in association with the RAAF Antarctic Flight and the name has been in continuous use since that time. The name was approved."</aadc:named_for>
